# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site configuration.  Edit this once, everything else reads from here.
#
# Every script and Makefile target sources this file, so you only ever change
# paths and SLURM settings in one place.
#
# THIS COPY IS CONFIGURED FOR JURECA (project training2635).
# The kit was built, and the `large` model pre-trained, on JUPITER; each JUPITER
# value is kept in the comment beside its replacement so the move can be read.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
# geoarches needs Python >=3.11,<3.13.
PYTHON_MODULE="Python/3.12.3"

# --- SLURM ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Taken from the job scripts the other training2635 challenges already run on
# JURECA, not guessed: --account=training2635, --partition=dc-gpu,
# --cpus-per-task=12.
SLURM_ACCOUNT="training2635"    # JUPITER was: hclimrep
SLURM_PARTITION="dc-gpu"        # JUPITER was: booster (4x GH200, 288 cores)
SLURM_GPUS_PER_NODE=4
SLURM_CPUS_PER_TASK=12          # JUPITER was: 72

# --- Data -------------------------------------------------------------------
# JUPITER's /e/data1 and /e/scratch are that machine's Exascale filesystems and
# are NOT mounted on JURECA, so everything the kit reads was copied under
# /p/scratch/training2635 and every path below points there.
#
# Raw GLORYS, regridded to 1 degree.  Only scripts/prepare_glorys.py reads it,
# and you do not need it -- the prepared files below are already here.  The raw
# archive (640 GB) was deliberately NOT copied, so this path does not exist and
# `make prep-data` cannot run until somebody stages it.
GLORYS_RAW="/p/scratch/training2635/4_ocean_ai/nowak2/glorys_1deg_raw_NOT_COPIED"

# Where prepared (yearly, level-subset) netCDF files live.  92 GB, copied.
DATA_ROOT="/p/scratch/training2635/4_ocean_ai/nowak2/hackathon-ocean-sea-ice/data"
GLORYS_PREPPED="${DATA_ROOT}/glorys_1deg_prepped"

# Optional atmospheric forcing (only covers ~2024 -- see docs/05_coupling.md).
# 833 MB, copied out of JUPITER's /e/data1 into the kit's own data directory.
IFS_FORCING="${DATA_ROOT}/ifs_1deg"

# --- Experiment output ------------------------------------------------------
# geoarches writes checkpoints to ${exp_dir} = modelstore/<name> relative to CWD.
# Only partly honoured, so leave it alone: the evaluation pipeline's run lookup
# reads it, but geoarches' own load_module hardcodes `modelstore/`. Pointing it
# elsewhere finds a run and then fails to load it. To use checkpoints from
# another checkout, symlink or copy them into modelstore/ instead.
MODELSTORE="modelstore"
EVALSTORE="evalstore"

# --- Data splits (years) ----------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately NO split setting here.  The splits are
#
#     train 1993-2018 / val 2019-2020 / test 2021-2023 / holdout 2024-2025
#
# and they live in SPLIT_YEARS in oceanarches/dataloaders/glorys.py, which is the
# only thing the dataloader's filename filters read.  This file used to carry a
# TRAIN_YEARS/VAL_YEARS/TEST_YEARS/HOLDOUT_YEARS block that nothing read, so
# editing TEST_YEARS changed nothing about the split your score is computed on.
# Change SPLIT_YEARS instead.
